    "narrative": "The path to victory today hinges on **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (81.14) and **Bryce Harper** (68.36), our clear offensive anchors. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Schultz, where his elite contact profile and favorable spot in the #3 hole provide our strongest floor-to-ceiling ratio. Meanwhile, **Bryce Harper** enters the slate with an impressive .388 xwOBA, and despite a 33% rain risk in his contest against Soriano, his offensive efficiency remains too high to bench. **Jung Hoo Lee** also earns a strong recommendation at 64.09; his matchup against Montero allows him to leverage his dynamic platoon advantage and a prime #2 batting order position to contribute meaningfully across our primary categories.\n\nStrategic volatility is centered on the trio of **Luis Arraez**, **Justin Crawford**, and **Bryce Harper**, all of whom face Soriano under a 33% threat of precipitation. While the potential for a rainout is a legitimate concern, their individual scores\u2014particularly the 60.82 for **Luis Arraez**\u2014compel us to keep them active. On the bench, **Lawrence Butler** was the most difficult exclusion. His 44.65 score reflects a favorable park factor, but he ultimately fell short of the threshold because his platoon disadvantage against Tolle suppressed his raw output compared to the efficiency of our active OF rotation. We are also monitoring the lineups for **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Daulton Varsho**; while current projections account for assumed positions, any deviation in their order could recalibrate their daily efficiency scores, particularly for **Gleyber Torres**, whose current score of 53.99 is already sensitive to his #2 spot.",
